From: h0cheung <hcheunh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: describe Elden UFS MCQ resources

Elden's stock SunP device tree describes MCQ SQD at 0x1da5000 (0x2000
bytes), vendor status at 0x1da4000 (0x10 bytes), and ITS device ID 0x60.
The controller's QCFGPTR 0xe0 places its MCQ configuration at
0x1d84000 + 0xe0 * 0x200 = 0x1da0000. These match the runtime doorbell
and vendor-status offsets used by the pinned Freedom UFS driver.

Translate them into that driver's std/mcq resource layout. The 0x7000
MCQ window covers configuration, vendor status and the stock SQD range;
the existing separate ICE window ends at the MCQ base and is unchanged.
Keep the override on the Elden board instead of all SM8750 systems.

Link: https://github.com/mydanyi/armadaos-freedom/tree/244b74516d99d06cb0518609ce4b842ab278be8a
Link: https://github.com/mydanyi/armadaos-freedom/blob/244b74516d99d06cb0518609ce4b842ab278be8a/packages/kernel/patches/0222-arm64-dts-qcom-kaanapali-describe-ufs-mcq.patch
Signed-off-by: h0cheung <hcheunh@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-lenovo-elden.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-lenovo-elden.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-lenovo-elden.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-lenovo-elden.dts
@@ -2376,6 +2376,11 @@
 };
 
 &ufs_mem_hc {
+	reg = <0x0 0x01d84000 0x0 0x3000>,
+	      <0x0 0x01da0000 0x0 0x7000>;
+	reg-names = "std", "mcq";
+	msi-parent = <&gic_its 0x60>;
+
 	reset-gpios = <&tlmm 215 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 
 	vcc-supply = <&vreg_l17b_2p5>;
